oil to hold it  in place  finally top it up with grated cheese and  bake in the oven for 20 to 25 minutes  and your eggs are cooked through and  golden brown serve hot this pepper  quiche  are absolutely delicious they are so  fluffy low in color and packed with  high-quality protein and also vegetables  so bring some color to the table and  make this quiche in pepper cups another  of my favorite dish is kiss ideas but it  is not always the healthiest option  especially if it's loaded with lots of  cheese and it can be very high in  calories so instead of making the  traditional quesadillas let's make it  open-faced which means lower calorie per  slice we want to top it out with lots of  vegetables and only sprinkle with a  light amount of cheese so for each  quesadilla when you'll need are one  medium whole grain tortilla 2x one cup  of fresh baby spinach quarter cup of  onions diced cortico of bell pepper  diced quarter cup of any cheese grated  about two tablespoons of black olives  sliced one teaspoon of olive oil half a  teaspoon of cayenne pepper and salt and  pepper to taste  preheat the oven to 180 degrees Celsius  or 350 degrees Fahrenheit so let's start  by prepping the eggs break and scramble  the eggs in a small bowl season with  cayenne pepper and salt and pepper set  aside hits olive oil over medium low  heat stir fry the onions and bell pepper  for one to two minutes until fragrant  then add the spinach and cook for  another one to two minutes until wilted  pour in the eggs and cook very quickly  until the eggs are just set only for  about 1 minutes we don't want to  overcook as the eggs will finish cooking  in the oven so remove from heat and set  aside line a baking tray with parchment  paper and place one tortilla top it up  with the scrambled egg mixture some  olives and sprinkle with cheese then  place in the oven and cook very quickly  just for 5 to 6 minutes until cheese is  melted and transfer the quesadilla to a  cutting board to cool down for a couple  of minutes and slice into 6 equal  portions serve warm this is such a great  and light dish to be shared it is  crunchy crispy and cheesy at the same  time it is just like a thin crust pizza  and each slice is under 100 calories the  best part is you can choose to top it up  with any toppings of your choice you can  even serve it as a starter or even as a  finger food so you got to try it and  finally why not give the ordinary egg  and toast a quick make over I tend to  have egg and toast very regularly for my  breakfast and sometimes it is nice to  put in a little bit more effort to make  breakfast and look pretty it is pleasing  to the eyes it will be pleasing to the  tummy and I am sure your family and kids  will love it so to make egg in a basket  you only need 2 thick slices of whole  grain bread 2 eggs 1 TSP of olive oil a  pinch of salt and pepper and also a  large cookie cutter break each egg into  a small bowl set aside then use the  cookie cutter cut out the center of each  bread slice in a non-stick pan hits  olive oil over medium low heat we want  to toast the bread slices and cut outs  on one side until golden brown then turn  the bread pieces over and gently pour  each egg into the center of each bread  slice  the pan and allow the eggs to cook  slowly for four to five minutes until  the whites are completely set and the  yolks begin to thicken but are in hot  then season with salt and pepper and  serve immediately with the cut outs  I just love to slice into the runny yolk  don't you this dish is packed with both  carbs and protein to sustain your energy  level it also makes a great post-workout  snack I love pretty looking breakfasts  because it puts a smile on my face  so guys start your morning by having a  bigger and more satisfying breakfast so  that you won't have the urge to snack as  often throughout the day it will help to  manage your appetite which also helps to  maintain a healthy weight long term so  this recipes are also great for lunch or  dinner so make them share the recipes  with your friends let me know which is  your favorite in the comments below and  don't forget to snap pictures of your  creation and share them with me on  Facebook or Instagram all the best so if  you want to become a certified personal  trainer just like me you can do so by  signing up to the National Academy of  Sports Medicine &amp; ASM online personal  training costs they are currently  offering a 14-day free trial and you'll  get to learn more about nutrition  creating a personalized fitness program  and also skills to understand your  clients so be sure to click on the link  in my description box to get more  information and share this
 

